# UTF-8 and naming

Folder names stay as they are (`common/`, `compiler/`, …). **Crate** and **Ada package** names do not.

## Crate names

Every Alire crate name starts with `lovelace`, in any folder. The `.gpr` file name matches the crate.

| Folder | Crate |
|---|---|
| `common/` | `lovelace_common` |
| `common/tests` | `lovelace_common_tests` |
| `lir/` | `lovelace_lir` |
| `compiler/` | `lovelace_compiler` |
| `tooling/` | `lovelace_tooling` |
| `format/` | `lovelace_format` |
| `alexandria/` | `lovelace_alexandria` |
| `hypatia/` | `lovelace_hypatia` |
| `jit/` | `lovelace_jit` |
| `augusta/` (native Ada, when created) | `lovelace_augusta` |
| `lovelace/` | `lovelace` (CLI executable) |
| repo root | `lovelace_workspace` |

Pin paths stay folder-relative (`common`, `../common`). Nested tests: `lovelace_<component>_tests`.

## Package names

Every Ada package starts with `Lovelace`.

**Library crates** use a second-level child named for that crate (folder / crate suffix, Mixed_Case), then further children under it. Do **not** hang units directly off `Lovelace` except the crate namespace itself.

| Crate | Package prefix | Example |
|---|---|---|
| `lovelace_common` | `Lovelace.Common` | `Lovelace.Common.Utf_8`, `Lovelace.Common.Regex` |
| `lovelace_lir` | `Lovelace.Lir` | `Lovelace.Lir.…` |
| `lovelace_compiler` | `Lovelace.Compiler` | `Lovelace.Compiler.…` |
| `lovelace_tooling` | `Lovelace.Tooling` | `Lovelace.Tooling.…` |
| `lovelace_format` | `Lovelace.Format` | `Lovelace.Format.…` |
| `lovelace_alexandria` | `Lovelace.Alexandria` | `Lovelace.Alexandria.…` |
| `lovelace_hypatia` | `Lovelace.Hypatia` | `Lovelace.Hypatia.…` |
| `lovelace_jit` | `Lovelace.Jit` | `Lovelace.Jit.…` |
| `lovelace_augusta` | `Lovelace.Augusta` | `Lovelace.Augusta.…` |
| `lovelace_common_tests` | `Lovelace.Common.Tests` | AUnit drivers under that prefix |

Root `package Lovelace` lives in `lovelace_common` so library children can exist. It is not a place for regex, UTF-8, or other crate logic (`Lovelace.Utf_8` is wrong; use `Lovelace.Common.Utf_8`).

**CLI crate `lovelace`:** only the root `procedure Lovelace` (no `Lovelace.Lovelace` and no extra `Lovelace.*` packages in that crate). `procedure Lovelace` in `lovelace/src/lovelace.adb` **must** become a child (e.g. `Lovelace.Main`) **before** the CLI crate depends on `lovelace_common` (parent/child name clash). Do not rename that procedure until the CLI is wired to `lovelace_common`.

## UTF-8

- Host string manipulation uses UTF-8. Ada `String` / `Unbounded_String` are UTF-8 **byte** sequences, not Latin-1 code units. Do not treat `Character` as a Lovelace character.
- Lovelace **string** literals are stored as UTF-8. Lovelace **character** literals are one Unicode scalar in 4 bytes (`Wide_Wide_Character` / a `Code_Point` subtype).
- `.love` and Ada sources are UTF-8 (identifiers and literals may include emoji). GNAT: `-gnatW8` on the shared host switch list.
